  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43341148",
      "title": "Creating a New Lucia Auth Instance",
      "lectureOrder": 213,
      "videoOrder": 199,
      "sourceHash": "767d09271d2f3300cefc5e7ce701882a21d6f8d3e07609aaa103dcec3a8425ff",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 3.27,
          "en": "So now that we did install Lucia,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.27,
          "end": 4.77,
          "en": "let's get started using it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.77,
          "end": 8.61,
          "en": "so that we can soon create such auth sessions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.61,
          "end": 11.943,
          "en": "and use them to identify authenticated users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 15.54,
          "en": "For that, I'll go to the lib folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.54,
          "end": 19.86,
          "en": "and in there I'll add a auth.js file now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.86,
          "end": 21.96,
          "en": "And it's now in this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.96,
          "end": 25.47,
          "en": "where I'll create a new constant called lucia.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.47,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "The name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 30.63,
          "en": "but it should store a new object that's created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.63,
          "end": 33.303,
          "en": "with help of the Lucia constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.86,
          "end": 36.78,
          "en": "And for that you actually need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.78,
          "end": 41.78,
          "en": "to import Lucia from this Lucia package, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.7,
          "end": 46.74,
          "en": "Now this constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.74,
          "end": 48.57,
          "en": "then needs a couple of arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.57,
          "end": 52.11,
          "en": "For example, it needs an adapter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.11,
          "end": 57.11,
          "en": "which will tell Lucia where and how to store those sessions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.6,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "That's why we installed that other package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "this @lucia-auth/adapter-sqlite package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 70.093,
          "en": "from which we can now import the BetterSqlite3Adapter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.05,
          "end": 76.8,
          "en": "With that imported, we can create a new adapter object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.8,
          "end": 78.9,
          "en": "by constructing this BetterSqlite3Adapter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 84.53999999999999,
          "en": "And to this adapter, we need to pass a handle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 84.53999999999999,
          "end": 88.44,
          "en": "to our BetterSqlite3.Database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.44,
          "end": 92.07,
          "en": "And conveniently we have that in the db.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.07,
          "end": 96.6,
          "en": "There I'm creating such a better-sqlite3 database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 96.6,
          "end": 99.36,
          "en": "and I'm then exporting that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 99.36,
          "end": 102.99000000000001,
          "en": "So therefore we can easily use that database here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 102.99000000000001,
          "end": 106.28999999999999,
          "en": "by importing it, like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 106.28999999999999,
          "end": 108.87,
          "en": "and by then assigning it as a first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.87,
          "end": 113.00999999999999,
          "en": "to this BetterSqlite3Adapter constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.00999999999999,
          "end": 116.78999999999999,
          "en": "And then as a second argument for this constructor here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 116.78999999999999,
          "end": 119.1,
          "en": "we can pass a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.1,
          "end": 121.98,
          "en": "where you can tell this adapter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.98,
          "end": 124.35,
          "en": "and therefore in the end, Lucia,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 129.35,
          "en": "what the table name of your users' database table will be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 130.14,
          "end": 131.97,
          "en": "And in my case, it's users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 131.97,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "because in a db.js file, I'm creating a user's table here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 137.88,
          "en": "for storing the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.88,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "and Lucia needs to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 143.043,
          "en": "in which database table you do store your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.97,
          "end": 146.34,
          "en": "And it also needs to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.34,
          "end": 148.44,
          "en": "where you are storing your sessions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.44,
          "end": 151.47,
          "en": "or where it should store the sessions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.47,
          "end": 153.72,
          "en": "what the name of the table in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.72,
          "end": 157.53,
          "en": "where those sessions should be stored will be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.53,
          "end": 161.91,
          "en": "And in my case, it should be this sessions table here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.91,
          "end": 164.52,
          "en": "So the table name is sessions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.52,
          "end": 166.713,
          "en": "That's what I'll assign here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.78,
          "end": 170.25,
          "en": "With that we have an adapter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.25,
          "end": 172.82999999999998,
          "en": "and that's now the first argument we must pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.82999999999998,
          "end": 174.903,
          "en": "to that Lucia constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.16,
          "end": 178.89,
          "en": "Then you can also pass a configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.89,
          "end": 182.16,
          "en": "to that constructor function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.16,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "And there you can configure various things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 188.37,
          "en": "but for us here, it's the sessionCookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.37,
          "end": 189.73,
          "en": "That's important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.59,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "because Lucia will automatically create that cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 196.11,
          "en": "that contains the session ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.11,
          "end": 199.74,
          "en": "because it's also Lucia that creates the session.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.74,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "But we can now configure that cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 206.79,
          "en": "And for example, when using Lucia in a NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 206.79,
          "end": 210.51,
          "en": "you should set expires to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.51,
          "end": 214.17000000000002,
          "en": "That's something you learn in the Lucia documentation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 214.17000000000002,
          "end": 217.53,
          "en": "And we can also add some attributes to that cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 217.53,
          "end": 220.07999999999998,
          "en": "And specifically, I wanna set this cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.07999999999998,
          "end": 223.56,
          "en": "to only work on HTTPS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.56,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "if we're running this app in production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 229.77,
          "en": "So if the NODE_ENV environment variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 229.77,
          "end": 231.45,
          "en": "which is set automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.45,
          "end": 235.07999999999998,
          "en": "by pretty much all hosting providers to production",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 235.07999999999998,
          "end": 237.48,
          "en": "if the app is running in production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 237.48,
          "end": 240.48,
          "en": "if that environment variable holds a value of production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 240.48,
          "end": 242.85,
          "en": "which means we're not running the app locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.85,
          "end": 245.91,
          "en": "during development, but instead we now did deploy it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.91,
          "end": 248.88,
          "en": "And in that case, I want to enforce this cookie",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.88,
          "end": 251.613,
          "en": "to only work across HTTPS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.72,
          "end": 254.28,
          "en": "But that's then it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.28,
          "end": 257.31,
          "en": "That's how we create a new Lucia instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.31,
          "end": 259.83,
          "en": "and we can now use that instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.83,
          "end": 262.98,
          "en": "to then create sessions and session cookies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 266.76,
          "en": "and to validate incoming requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.76,
          "end": 269.943,
          "en": "and see if they have a valid session cookie.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
